@startbpmn BP03_MaintainRoutines
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP03_MaintainRoutines.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP03_MaintainRoutines.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - a routine has NO theme: maintenance rather than achievement, so nothing about a life area
'     attaches to it: BR-02, SA 2026-10-13 ("For Routines I don't care about themes, really",
'     over the optional affiliation of 2026-10-11). Until then this process entered through a
'     section of the Themes tab - a life area, or Unthemed - and the editor carried a life area
'     field; both are gone
'   - routines therefore have a home of their own, the Routines view, and BR-10's one deliberate
'     exception is gone with the affiliation: BR-10, UX-14, SA 2026-10-13
'   - a routine is not archivable; it is paused or deleted: BR-23
'   - four recurrence patterns, no fifth, plus preferred days: BR-94
'   - the schedule computes due and overdue and never creates a task: BR-91
'   - only selecting a routine creates its task, and at most one outstanding: BR-42
'   - deleting a routine offers a cascade over the occurrences it already produced: BR-16
'   - that cascade is declinable, so it is off by default: BR-19
'   - WHICH cascade the gesture offers is not business relevant: one choice - a valid option, or
'     no deletion - and the options are the disclosure's content (BP03.06): SA 2026-10-11
'   - a paused routine cannot be selected for a day: BR-43
'   - a paused routine is neither due nor overdue, and paused days never become overdue: BR-91
'   - one editor per entity serves creating and editing alike, and nothing separated the two
'     chains but the fields they stored, so they are ONE request: UX-04, SA 2026-10-11. Call site
'     BP03.03 (Amend a routine) is RETIRED, its id never reused, and BP03.02 is the one editing
'     request
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - a step never enumerates the fields a request stores: which fields the entity carries is
'     a Detail Design matter and is not known yet, so the step names the act and its subject
'     only: SA 2026-10-14
'   - the box carries the act's own word, not the generic edit: the user DEFINES a routine, which
'     is Intent's own word for it; the operation keeps its own: SA 2026-10-16
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'
'   - the chain's NAME said "a section's routines", from when routines sat under a life area. A
'     routine carries no theme and the view offers one list, so the name is the routines' and
'     nothing else. The id is untouched, a name being descriptive and an id never renamed:
'     BR-02, BR-10, ADR-066, SA 2026-10-17 ("drop stale sub BP")
'
' Call-site collapsing: pause and resume are one request with two variations, the way setting an
' activity's state is one act in BP18. Defining and amending stay separate: one creates, the
' other changes what exists.

pool "User" {
  start "A routine needs attention"
  :Work a routine;
  rule BR-118

  if "What needs doing?" then "add or change a routine"
    :Define the routine;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the routine;
    send "Edit a routine" to editIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as recorded
    note "The schedule is a recurrence pattern plus preferred days: it says when the routine is due, and never puts work on a board."
    end "Routine recorded"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "put one on hold, or take it off hold"
    :Pause or resume the routine;
    send "Pause or resume a routine" to activeIn
    receive "The pause-or-resume outcome" as activeSet
    end "Routine paused or resumed"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "reorder them"
    :Order a routine;
    send "Reorder routines" to reorderIn
    receive "The ordering outcome" as reordered
    end "Routines ordered"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "retire one for good"
    :Delete a routine;
    send "See what deleting a routine takes" to impactIn
    receive "What the deletion will take" as impact
    if "Approve what the deletion takes?" rule BR-16 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      :Confirm the deletion;
      send "Delete a routine" to deleteIn
      receive "The deletion outcome" as deleted
      note "The routine stops producing new ones either way; the occurrences it already produced go or stay on Chores."
    else "reject"
      end "Deletion abandoned"
    endif
    end "Routine deleted"
  endif
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Routine submitted" as editIn
  call "BP03.02_EditRoutine" "Edit a routine" {
    :Store the edit;
    rule BR-94
    rule BR-02
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to recorded
  note "A routine carries no life area. The recurrence is Daily, Weekly, Monthly or Yearly."
  end "Routine answered"

  messageStart "Pause or resume submitted" as activeIn
  call "BP03.04_SetRoutineActive" "Pause or resume a routine" {
    :Apply the pause or the resume;
    :Report the outcome;
    rule BR-43
  }
  send "The pause-or-resume outcome" to activeSet
  note "A paused routine leaves the focus selectables and the due computation, and returns to both on resume."
  end "Pause or resume answered"

  messageStart "Routine reordering requested" as reorderIn
  call "BP03.05_ReorderRoutines" "Reorder routines" {
    :Apply the new order;
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The ordering outcome" to reordered
  end "Reordering answered"

  messageStart "Deletion impact requested" as impactIn
  call "BP03.06_ReadTheDeletionImpact" "See what deleting a routine takes" {
    :Report what the deletion will take, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-12
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-117
  }
  send "What the deletion will take" to impact
  note "The occurrences are a declinable cascade, so it starts off. Declining leaves them on Chores and stops the routine producing new ones."
  end "Impact answered"

  messageStart "Routine deletion requested" as deleteIn
  call "BP03.07_DeleteRoutine" "Delete a routine" {
    :Delete confirmed items;
    rule BR-16
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The deletion outcome" to deleted
  note "The request carries the cascade the user approved."
  end "Deletion answered"
}

@endbpmn
